1
00:00:00,449 --> 00:00:02,734
An AI agent calls a payment tool.

2
00:00:02,734 --> 00:00:04,833
The tool replies: ok.

3
00:00:04,833 --> 00:00:06,402
Did the money actually move?

4
00:00:06,402 --> 00:00:08,501
The same request can get the same reply in

5
00:00:08,501 --> 00:00:09,892
different hidden worlds.

6
00:00:09,892 --> 00:00:12,381
Sometimes ok means nothing was paid at all.

7
00:00:12,381 --> 00:00:14,940
Sometimes a timeout means you already paid, and

8
00:00:14,940 --> 00:00:17,521
a blind retry pays the supplier twice.

9
00:00:18,321 --> 00:00:20,680
So we built ActionProof, a benchmark of these

10
00:00:20,680 --> 00:00:24,356
silent faults. On 440 locked tasks, an agent

11
00:00:24,356 --> 00:00:26,986
that trusts the reply falsely reports success

12
00:00:26,986 --> 00:00:28,637
86 percent of the time.

13
00:00:28,637 --> 00:00:30,099
The fix is obvious:

14
00:00:30,099 --> 00:00:32,244
read the record back before you say done.

15
00:00:33,044 --> 00:00:35,403
And a three billion parameter Cohere model can

16
00:00:35,403 --> 00:00:37,605
learn it. Here is a recorded run on our live

17
00:00:37,605 --> 00:00:40,424
Space. The tool says ok, but nothing was

18
00:00:40,424 --> 00:00:42,605
written. The reply-trusting script reports

19
00:00:42,605 --> 00:00:44,858
done. Our trained agent reads the payment

20
00:00:44,858 --> 00:00:47,145
ledger, finds it empty, pays again with the

21
00:00:47,145 --> 00:00:50,235
same idempotency key, and confirms exactly one

22
00:00:50,235 --> 00:00:51,036
payment.

23
00:00:51,836 --> 00:00:53,640
But training that habit exposed something

24
00:00:53,640 --> 00:00:55,642
deeper about how we train agents.

25
00:00:55,642 --> 00:00:58,543
With GRPO, standard GRPO, the agent should

26
00:00:58,543 --> 00:01:00,182
learn to check whenever checking is worth its

27
00:01:00,182 --> 00:01:02,576
cost. Often, it does not.

28
00:01:02,576 --> 00:01:04,345
And the cause is not the reward.

29
00:01:04,345 --> 00:01:07,056
It is how rewards are scaled inside the group.

30
00:01:07,856 --> 00:01:10,474
In GRPO, all the rollouts of one task share the

31
00:01:10,474 --> 00:01:13,245
same hidden world: the same database, the same

32
00:01:13,245 --> 00:01:15,813
silent fault. Rewards are then standardised

33
00:01:15,813 --> 00:01:18,172
inside that group. That division cancels each

34
00:01:18,172 --> 00:01:20,306
hidden state's stakes, how much a missed fault

35
00:01:20,306 --> 00:01:23,125
actually costs. What survives is a vote:

36
00:01:23,125 --> 00:01:25,860
which states prefer checking, not by how much.

37
00:01:25,860 --> 00:01:28,561
So a rare, expensive fault can be outvoted by a

38
00:01:28,561 --> 00:01:30,624
cheap, common clean case.

39
00:01:31,424 --> 00:01:33,428
We registered the predictions before testing

40
00:01:33,428 --> 00:01:36,374
them, on 731 held-out cells.

41
00:01:36,374 --> 00:01:39,876
The theory predicts what GRPO learns in all 721

42
00:01:39,876 --> 00:01:43,142
decided cells, including all 77 where the vote

43
00:01:43,142 --> 00:01:44,569
and the value disagree.

44
00:01:44,569 --> 00:01:47,105
One registered hypothesis failed, and one could

45
00:01:47,105 --> 00:01:49,616
not be tested. We report both.

46
00:01:50,416 --> 00:01:52,845
Then we tested it on the real agent, five seeds

47
00:01:52,845 --> 00:01:55,684
per arm. Every GRPO seed ends exactly where it

48
00:01:55,684 --> 00:01:57,476
started: it never reads.

49
00:01:57,476 --> 00:01:59,729
Remove the group standard deviation, and the

50
00:01:59,729 --> 00:02:01,462
same model learns to check:

51
00:02:01,462 --> 00:02:06,887
verified completion rises from 0.687 to 0.807.

52
00:02:06,887 --> 00:02:08,290
Plus twelve points.

53
00:02:08,290 --> 00:02:10,165
And we say what this does not show:

54
00:02:10,165 --> 00:02:12,972
the GRPO arm is degenerate, so the p value is

55
00:02:12,972 --> 00:02:14,138
the test's floor.

56
00:02:14,938 --> 00:02:17,285
Every number you have seen resolves to one file

57
00:02:17,285 --> 00:02:19,428
and one command. A fresh public clone

58
00:02:19,428 --> 00:02:23,367
re-derived all 899 claims, with zero failures,

59
00:02:23,367 --> 00:02:24,734
and no GPU.

60
00:02:25,534 --> 00:02:28,267
ActionProof. When you train agents to check,

61
00:02:28,267 --> 00:02:29,693
keep the stakes in the group.
